= American Weapons Embargo

Congress has suspended arms deliveries to Turkey. The embargo that took effect on 5 February 1975 interrupts the flow of equipment and spare parts on which our forces have depended. The army, navy and air force remain capable, but maintaining readiness will be harder until new sources of supply can be secured.

Army, naval and aerial strength each fall by 0.15.

[? if cyprus_poppy_penalty == 1 or hashas_done == 1 : **Additional economic sanctions:** Washington has also restricted economic assistance in response to the lifting of the poppy cultivation ban. Foreign-exchange pressure rises by 25 and the growth modifier falls by 0.5. This remains the historical arms-embargo path, not the alternative delayed-ceasefire event. ?]

